exports[`English marketing copy llms.txt is the recorded text 1`] = `
"# LumenWipe

> Closes a Stellar account end to end and recovers the XLM locked in its reserves: it removes signers, data entries, offers and trustlines, exits Soroban DeFi positions, converts leftovers to XLM, and merges the account.

Live means available on mainnet. Testnet only means it runs on Stellar testnet and not yet on mainnet.

## Trust model

Your secret key never reaches a LumenWipe server, and LumenWipe does not store or log it: you sign in your browser, through your wallet or a key held in memory for this session only.

The LumenWipe API reads your account and builds each unsigned transaction. Before you sign, your browser decodes it and checks its operations and destination against what you entered; if they do not match, it stops before asking you to sign.

Two keys sign on the server, and neither can sign for your account.

- Relay account key: In an exchange close, it co-signs only a two-operation transaction: your account's merge into the relay account and an XLM payment from it in the same transaction. Before you sign, your browser checks that this payment goes to the exchange address you typed. Testnet only today.
- Fee-sponsor key: When a fee is sponsored, it signs only the fee-bump envelope that pays the network fee for a transaction you already signed, and cannot change that transaction. Testnet only today.

The browser check is open source: https://github.com/LumenWipe/lumenwipe/blob/main/apps/web/lib/stellar/verify.ts

## Features

- Classic account close (Live): Removes signers, data entries, offers and trustlines, converts or returns leftover assets, and merges the account into a wallet you choose.
- Soroban DeFi exits (Live): Detects positions through OctoPos and exits each one with its own protocol adapter, repaying loans, withdrawing liquidity and unstaking, before the trustline is removed.
- Exchange-compatible close (Testnet only): A shared relay account receives the merge and pays the balance on to an exchange deposit address, with the memo the exchange requires, in the same transaction.
- Sponsored fees (Testnet only): Pays the network fee for an account sitting at its minimum balance, through a fee-bump envelope around the transaction you signed.
- Allowance inspector (Live): See every token approval your account granted to DeFi contracts, and revoke risky ones, even without closing.
- Resumable sessions (Live): Close the tab mid-flow and resume in the same browser: the account is re-read and a fresh plan covers only what is left, so confirmed work is not repeated.
- Deterministic, auditable plan (Live): The same account state always produces the same ordered plan: testable, reviewable, never built on stale data.

## Protocol exits

- Blend: Live
- Soroswap: Live
- Aquarius: Live
- Phoenix: Live
- FxDAO: Testnet only

## Links

- [Security](https://lumenwipe.com/security): the trust model and the keys on the server
- [Security reports](https://lumenwipe.com/security/reports): every published security report, and the self-assessed threat model and remediation plan until one exists
- [How it works](https://lumenwipe.com/how-it-works): the close, step by step
- [FAQ](https://lumenwipe.com/faq)
- [Documentation](https://docs.lumenwipe.com)
- [Supported protocols, assets and wallets](https://docs.lumenwipe.com/reference/supported)
- [API reference](https://docs.lumenwipe.com/api-reference/introduction)
- [Source code](https://github.com/LumenWipe/lumenwipe)
"
`;
